# cluster.env.example — template for the SVC-07 automated installer (Developer B)
#
# Copy this to an environment-specific, GITIGNORED cluster env file and fill in
# the real values for YOUR Proxmox cluster. NEVER commit the copy, and never put
# a real endpoint, token, or hostname in this `.example` file — every value
# below is an obviously-fake placeholder only.
#
#   cp cluster.env.example cluster.dev.env      # local / development cluster
#   $EDITOR cluster.dev.env                      # fill in real values
#
# then run the installer against it:
#
#   ~/venv/devinfra/bin/ansible-playbook \
#     -i ansible/inventory/localhost.yml \
#     ansible/playbooks/svc-07-bootstrap.yml \
#     -e cluster_env_file=cluster.dev.env
#
# The installer defaults to `cluster.env` when `-e cluster_env_file=...` is not
# supplied, so `cp cluster.env.example cluster.env` also works. Supported env
# files: cluster.env (default), cluster.dev.env, cluster.acc.env, cluster.prod.env.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ALIASES: each logical variable is accepted under EITHER of two prefixes —
# a `PROXMOX_`-prefixed form OR a `TF_VAR_`-prefixed form. Define exactly ONE
# of each pair. Defining BOTH aliases of the same variable with conflicting,
# non-empty values is a hard error at preflight (identical values resolve
# cleanly). The two commented forms are shown for each variable below; pick one,
# uncomment it, and fill in the value.
#
# SECURITY (security-standards.md):
#   * No secret is ever committed — the copied file is gitignored; keep it so.
#   * A Proxmox API token has the format:  <user>@<realm>!<token-id>=<uuid>
#   * The token MUST carry the SDN.Allocate privilege and be a least-privilege
#     terraform@pve-style token, never the built-in Administrator role.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ===========================================================================
# SDN / API — the SVC-07 automated installer core parameters. The
# platform-prerequisites-bootstrap orchestrator's `api` bucket reuses these to
# drive the platform-foundation Terraform apply.
# ===========================================================================

# --- Proxmox endpoint (MANDATORY) -------------------------------------------
# The BASE URL for the Proxmox VE API — host and port only, with NO API path
# (no trailing `/api2/json`) and no trailing slash. This matches the bpg/proxmox
# Terraform provider contract in providers.tf ("No trailing path beyond the
# host/port"); Phase-1 Preflight appends `/api2/json/...` itself, so supplying
# the path here would double it. Define ONE of the two alias forms:
PROXMOX_ENDPOINT="https://proxmox.example.invalid:8006"
#TF_VAR_proxmox_endpoint="https://proxmox.example.invalid:8006"

# --- Proxmox TLS verification (OPTIONAL) ------------------------------------
# TLS verification of the Proxmox API certificate defaults to OFF, because a
# homelab Proxmox host typically presents a SELF-SIGNED cert. This single
# default governs BOTH consumers so they cannot drift: Phase-1 Preflight's
# reachability checks AND the bpg/proxmox Terraform provider's `insecure`
# setting (the installer derives TF_VAR_proxmox_insecure = NOT validate_certs).
# There is NO cluster-env variable for this — to turn verification ON (e.g. a
# cluster presenting a trusted/CA-signed cert), pass the installer play var:
#   ~/venv/devinfra/bin/ansible-playbook ... -e svc07_proxmox_validate_certs=true

# --- Proxmox API token (MANDATORY) ------------------------------------------
# Never echoed by the installer, never committed. Define ONE of the two forms:
PROXMOX_API_TOKEN="terraform@pve!installer=CHANGE-ME-00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"
#TF_VAR_proxmox_api_token="terraform@pve!installer=CHANGE-ME-00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"

# --- Proxmox node name (MANDATORY) ------------------------------------------
# The target Proxmox node the two SVC-07 LXCs are created on. Define ONE form:
PROXMOX_NODE_NAME="your-node-name"
#TF_VAR_proxmox_node_name="your-node-name"

# --- LXC template (MANDATORY) -----------------------------------------------
# The pveam template id in `<datastore>:vztmpl/<file>` form. Define ONE form:
PROXMOX_LXC_TEMPLATE="local:vztmpl/debian-12-standard_12.7-1_amd64.tar.zst"
#TF_VAR_openbao_template_file_id="local:vztmpl/debian-12-standard_12.7-1_amd64.tar.zst"

# --- Datastore (OPTIONAL) ---------------------------------------------------
# The datastore the LXC rootfs is placed on. Leave BOTH forms unset to let the
# installer auto-detect (prefers `local-zfs`, falls back to `local-lvm`). To
# pin it explicitly and skip auto-detection, define ONE form:
#PROXMOX_DATASTORE_ID="local-zfs"
#TF_VAR_openbao_datastore_id="local-zfs"

# --- SSH public key file (OPTIONAL) -----------------------------------------
# Path to YOUR PUBLIC SSH key FILE. The installer reads this file and injects
# its contents into BOTH SVC-07 LXCs' root accounts at guest CREATION, so that
# Ansible (Phase 3, common.yml) can SSH into the freshly-provisioned guests.
# Without it the guests are created with NO authorized key and Ansible fails
# with "Permission denied (publickey,password)".
#
#   * PUBLIC key ONLY — point this at the `.pub` file, NEVER a private key.
#   * A leading `~` is expanded (e.g. ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub -> $HOME/.ssh/...).
#   * ABSENT (both forms unset) => an empty key list is passed => Terraform's
#     user_account block is omitted => the guests provision normally but are
#     SSH-UNREACHABLE until a key is supplied (the documented default).
#   * Applied ONLY at guest CREATION. If the guests already exist, a newly-set
#     key does NOT retro-fit — clean-slate re-provision (-e clean_slate=true)
#     and re-run so the key is injected at creation.
#
# This is member (c) of the "Proxmox connection settings derived from your
# cluster config" family alongside the endpoint and TLS toggle above. Define
# ONE of the two alias forms (obviously-fake placeholder path shown):
#PROXMOX_SSH_PUBLIC_KEY_FILE="~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub"
#TF_VAR_operator_ssh_public_key_file="~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub"
# (The SSH identity file above is REUSED by the dev-machine bucket below for the
#  `~/.ssh/config` identity pin — it is not duplicated in the Dev machine section.)

# ===========================================================================
# Host prep (bootstrap) — consumed by the platform-prerequisites-bootstrap
# orchestrator's `host` bucket ONLY (ansible/playbooks/platform-bootstrap.yml).
# Every value in this section is OPTIONAL to cluster_env.py itself; the
# orchestrator decides which are required for the buckets you select and
# supplies the documented defaults when a key is absent. Placeholders only.
# ===========================================================================

# --- Proxmox host LAN IP (OPTIONAL; required by the host/devmachine buckets) -
# The Proxmox host's address ON YOUR LAN — used as the `ansible_host` for the
# host bucket (proxmox-hosts.yml) and as the `via` gateway in the dev-machine
# static route (`ip route add 10.0.<vlan>.0/24 via <this>`). Obviously-fake
# placeholder; define ONE alias form:
#PROXMOX_HOST_LAN_IP="192.0.2.10"
#TF_VAR_proxmox_host_lan_ip="192.0.2.10"

# --- Admin_Bootstrap_Credential (OPTIONAL; BOOTSTRAP-ONLY) ------------------
# A privileged Proxmox admin credential used ONLY by the opt-in PVE-identity
# step (`-e bootstrap_pve_identity=true`) to CREATE the least-privilege
# terraform@pve role/user/token. Supply EITHER an admin password OR an admin
# API token (not both). CRITICAL handling:
#   * BOOTSTRAP-ONLY: needed for the one-time identity mint, nothing else. Leave
#     BOTH unset for every routine (non-PVE-identity) run.
#   * no_log: the orchestrator marks every task touching these `no_log`; the
#     VALUE is NEVER echoed to stdout/stderr or any human-facing message, exactly
#     like PROXMOX_API_TOKEN.
#   * NEVER persisted, NEVER committed: the orchestrator does not write these
#     back into cluster.env; remove them from your copied file after a successful
#     PVE-identity bootstrap. This copied file is gitignored — keep it so.
# Define AT MOST one of these (obviously-fake placeholders):
#PROXMOX_ADMIN_PASSWORD="CHANGE-ME-bootstrap-only-admin-password"
#PROXMOX_ADMIN_TOKEN="root@pam!bootstrap=CHANGE-ME-00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000"

# --- Terraform identity ids (OPTIONAL; defaults shown) ----------------------
# Names for the least-privilege identity the PVE-identity step creates. When a
# key is ABSENT the orchestrator applies the default noted below.
#   PROXMOX_TERRAFORM_ROLE_ID   default: TerraformProv
#   PROXMOX_TERRAFORM_TOKEN_ID  default: installer
#PROXMOX_TERRAFORM_ROLE_ID="TerraformProv"
#PROXMOX_TERRAFORM_TOKEN_ID="installer"

# --- Template storage (OPTIONAL; default: local) ----------------------------
# The Proxmox storage the base LXC template is ensured/downloaded on via `pveam`
# (host bucket Ensure_Template step). Absent => the orchestrator defaults to
# `local`.
#PROXMOX_TEMPLATE_STORAGE="local"

# ===========================================================================
# Dev machine — consumed by the platform-prerequisites-bootstrap orchestrator's
# `devmachine` bucket (emit-by-default; applies only with `-e devmachine_apply=true`).
# The SSH identity file for the `~/.ssh/config` pin is the PROXMOX_SSH_PUBLIC_KEY_FILE
# defined in the SDN / API section above — it is NOT repeated here. Placeholders only.
# ===========================================================================

# --- Served VLAN ids (OPTIONAL; default: 20) --------------------------------
# The VLAN id(s) your workstation should be able to reach through the Proxmox
# host — drives the emitted `ip route add 10.0.<vlan>.0/24 ...` command(s).
# Comma-separated for several. Absent => the orchestrator defaults to `20`
# (the shared-services VLAN).
#PLATFORM_SERVED_VLAN_IDS="20"

# --- Admin source CIDR (OPTIONAL) -------------------------------------------
# The source CIDR permitted to reach the SDN gateway (feeds the host bucket's
# sdn_gateway role as `sdn_gateway_admin_source_cidr`). Obviously-fake
# placeholder — set to YOUR workstation/LAN CIDR:
#ADMIN_SOURCE_CIDR="192.0.2.0/24"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ORCHESTRATOR-WRITTEN VALUES — do not set these yourself.
#
#   * OPENBAO_ADMIN_TOKEN is NOT set by the operator. The SVC-07 installer WRITES
#     it back into this file (at mode 0600) at the end of a successful bootstrap,
#     capturing the platform-admin token minted in the one-time bootstrap window.
#
#   * PROXMOX_API_TOKEN is likewise WRITTEN BACK (at mode 0600) by the
#     platform-prerequisites-bootstrap orchestrator when the opt-in PVE-identity
#     step (`-e bootstrap_pve_identity=true`) MINTS the least-privilege
#     terraform@pve token. If you are running that step you may leave
#     PROXMOX_API_TOKEN unset above and let the orchestrator populate it; the
#     minted token's secret is never echoed, only persisted here at 0600.
#
# Do not add either by hand, and never commit the copied file once written back.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
